1. Lower Bound Computation Formulation
2. Further opportunities for Optimization. Relaxing Partial Marginal Constraints 
3. Let us consider the lower bound for \ud835\udc543error. As mentioned in Section 3.3, information about the marginals are enforced using linear constraints.
4. For a given AFD \ud835\udc4b\u2192\ud835\udc4d, the idea here is to drop some of these linear constraints on \ud835\udc4d("right-hand side ") with the same optimization goal.
5. This left us with an optimization sub-problem which can be efficiently and optimally solved greedily.
6. For the sub-problem for lower bound on \ud835\udc543error, the maximum value in each row needs to be maximized while the constraints on \ud835\udc4d are maintained.
7. As the joint distribution frequency matrix captures the read data, the maximum value in the row represents the current maximum value in the read data.
8. The rest of the values represent the current \ud835\udc543error.
