[all_together_subsections] parent=Data Model & Problem Definition sample=7 attempt=1/7
Here is the list of problems and their corresponding excerpts:

1. Problem Definitions
    excerpt: We define two broad classes of problems. Given a set of records of the DARE read, a tunable parameter θ, marginal distributions MAofA, an error measure (ε1, ε2 or ε3), an integer k, retrieve as a ranked list the top-k AFDs having the least errors (along with their respective error scores, if possible) from among all AFDs having exactly θ attributes in the left hand side (LHS).

2. Definition of Anytime Algorithms for AFDs
    excerpt: Before proposing our solutions to the above problems, we would like to define the notion of Anytime Algorithms in the context of computing AFDs. Our definition hinges on a few observations. For each of the proposed problems, the output is a set of AFDs. Let AFD(D) represent the set of output AFDs that are identified after reading the entire database D. We refer to this as the optimal output. Consider an algorithm that has only read part of the data-base, say D⊆, yet is able to output a set of AFDs, say AFD(D⊆), as the solution for the full database. Such an algorithm is called an Anytime Algorithm.
